[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datagen24/victual/pulls/985","id":4911178658,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUEWha88AAAABJLqjog","html_url":"https://github.com/datagen24/victual/pull/985","diff_url":"https://github.com/datagen24/victual/pull/985.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/datagen24/victual/pull/985.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datagen24/victual/issues/985","number":985,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"feat: tell an unknown stock value from a known zero (#774, part 2)","user":{"login":"datagen24","id":20876965,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwODc2OTY1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20876965?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/datagen24","html_url":"https://github.com/datagen24","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datagen24/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datagen24/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datagen24/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datagen24/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datagen24/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datagen24/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datagen24/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datagen24/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datagen24/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #774. Part 2 of 2, **stacked on #984**: merge #984 first, then this. The base branch is #984's, so this diff is part 2 only. Implements [ADR-0045](docs/adr/0045-an-unknown-stock-value-is-distinguishable-from-a-known-zero.md) option B and P2 for production gate **M2**. **ADR-0045 stays Proposed**; acceptance is a separate PR.\n\n## Meanings on the wire\n| Price state | API |\n|---|---|\n| Known zero (free) | `0` |\n| Unknown (never recorded, or a 0 that part 1 marked) | `null` |\n| Caller without `STOCK_PRICES_VIEW` | field absent |\n\nAn aggregate (`value`, `stock_value`) is the **known part**. A boolean, `value_incomplete` or `stock_value_incomplete`, says whether it is the whole. A parent's value and flag cover its own stock only (open question 1).\n\n## What changed\n- **Migration 0316**\n  - `stock_current.value_incomplete`, carried by `uihelper_stock_current_overview`; both of that view's literal UNION branches gain the `0`.\n  - D1: `products_price_history` and `products_average_price` count a known `0` and skip an unknown price.\n  - D2: `products_last_purchased.price` is `NULL` when no purchase has a known price. `products_current_price` falls back from an unknown or marked next-use price to the last known one (open question 2), and is `NULL` when there is none.\n  - D3: `recipes_pos_resolved.costs` is `NULL` for a position whose product has no known price.\n  - D4: `prices_incomplete` marks an unknown cost, not a zero one. A recipe with no position stays `1`, as before.\n  - Rebuilds both price caches, and adds the flags' `permission_fields` rows, also in `db/pgsql/prices-seed.sql`.\n- **API:** `GET /api/stock`, the volatile lists and both product details routes carry the flags, which are wire booleans in `WireBooleans`, `DOCUMENTED_BOOLEANS` and `CONVERSION_COVERAGE`.\n- **Raw rows (open question 10):** `FieldPolicy` maps a marked price to `null` on every raw stock and ledger row, before price redaction.\n- **P2 write paths**\n  - `purchase.js` sends `null` for a blank price and when price tracking is off.\n  - Self-production from a recipe with incomplete costs books `null`.\n  - Inventory correction now books `null` instead of `0` when no price is known, because `last_price` is `null` there under D2.\n- **Web UI:** the stock overview and the product card show a red ⓘ marker on an incomplete value, using one new string. The overview now shows a last or average price of `0` instead of hiding it.\n- **OpenAPI:** states the meanings on `value`, `stock_value`, `last_price`, `avg_price`, `current_price`, `StockEntry.price` and `StockLogEntry.price`, adds both flags, and states the parent scope.\n- **Difftest:** strips `value_incomplete` on the PostgreSQL side. Both views it touches had no matching column on the frozen SQLite line.\n\n## The M2 prerequisites\n1. **P2 and the import policy:** #984 covers them (marker, upgrade, import, report, `--legacy-zero-prices`).\n2. **Option B with the answers to open questions 2 and 4:** tests (a)–(e) and D2.\n3. **Client coordination (ADR-0024):** tracked under #891 / M7. victual-kit reads `nil` as \"no permission\" today, and `last_price`/`current_price` now become `null` for unknown prices. That change of meaning needs a coordinated client release.\n4. **Option A's requirements:** n/a.\n5. **Gate 5:** all flag rows and registry entries are present.\n6. **Parent scope:** `testAParentWithStockOnlyInItsSubProductsReportsItsOwnValue`.\n7. **D1–D4:** each has a targeted PHPUnit test and a pgTAP assertion, as the answer to open question 13 requires. The difftest views phase is unchanged, because its fixtures exercise none of them, as gate 7 predicted.\n\n## Breaking changes (0.5.0 release notes)\n- `last_price`, `current_price` and `oldest_price` are `null` where they were `0` for a product with no known price. Raw rows send `null` for a legacy-zero price.\n- `avg_price` and the price history now **include** known `0` (free) purchases, so averages can drop where a `0` used to be skipped.\n- Self-production and inventory corrections without a known price store `null` instead of `0`.\n- The flags are additive.\n\n## Contract snapshot diff, by path\nThe fixture gains an unpriced and a mixed product before the stock reads.\n- `GET /api/stock` and `/volatile`: `value_incomplete: boolean`. The new fixture products widen `description` and `product_group_id` to include `null`.\n- Both product details routes: `stock_value_incomplete: boolean`.\n- `products_last_purchased.price` and location entries' `price`: widened to include `null` (D2, and the unpriced fixture entry).\n- The self-production booking's `price`: `null`, from the P2 change for an incomplete recipe.\n\n## Tests\n- **`StockPriceSemanticsTest`** (15 tests, stocklocations phase): cases (a)–(f) on `/api/stock` and product details, the volatile flag, the parent, raw rows, the P2 write paths, and D1–D4. **13 fail on #984's code.** The two that pass are the redaction case and the purchase-with-no-price case, which were already true.\n- **pgTAP `039-price-readers.sql`:** 14 assertions. pgTAP 026's issue #629 case now expects `NULL` (D3); it expected `0` before.\n- **Browser probe `.devtools/frontend/price-semantics.js`**, wired into `frontend-security`: overview and product card markers, and a known-zero last price is shown. **Not run locally:** no host PHP or probe dependencies here, so CI is its first run.\n- **Full local `run-tests.sh all` passed:** `SUITE PASSED`, 35 phases. Staged Vale 0 new findings.\n\n## Not changed (deliberately)\n- **Influx:** the publisher reads `stock_log` directly, so a legacy-zero booking still publishes its stored `0.0`. Option B leaves Influx as it is.\n- **`mealplan.js`:** still turns a `null` last price into `0` for its cost arithmetic.\n- **The stock entries page (`uihelper_stock_entries`):** shows the stored `0` for a marked entry.\n- **Weighing:** goes through the same `last_price` as inventory correction, but has no test of its own.\n- **Not run:** the parity suite's `accepted.js` (not a gate) and PostgreSQL 15.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","created_at":"2026-10-18T17:22:59Z","updated_at":"2026-10-18T17:45:01Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"e93edb6c3f41836156db80b1913ad8f233af6b00","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datagen24/victual/pulls/985/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datage