l.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:datagen24/victual.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/datagen24/victual.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/datagen24/victual","homepage":"","size":70633,"stargazers_count":0,"watchers_count":0,"language":"PHP","has_issues":true,"has_projects":false,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":1,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":33,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":1,"open_issues":33,"watchers":0,"default_branch":"master"}},"_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/datagen24/victual/pulls/985"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/datagen24/victual/pull/985"},"issue":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/datagen24/victual/issues/985"},"comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/datagen24/victual/issues/985/comments"},"review_comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/datagen24/victual/pulls/985/comments"},"review_comment":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/datagen24/victual/pulls/comments{/number}"},"commits":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/datagen24/victual/pulls/985/commits"},"statuses":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/datagen24/victual/statuses/d3e3e03b6703fd08d94c4c26fa7b89a3e6e1c784"}},"author_association":"OWNER","auto_merge":null,"stack":{"id":2279962,"number":986,"base":{"ref":"master","sha":"d4e35751e6d8033eb930d573657d10ceb5e8c4d8"},"size":2,"position":2},"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datagen24/victual/pulls/984","id":4910947901,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUEWha88AAAABJLcePQ","html_url":"https://github.com/datagen24/victual/pull/984","diff_url":"https://github.com/datagen24/victual/pull/984.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/datagen24/victual/pull/984.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datagen24/victual/issues/984","number":984,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"feat: mark a stored price of 0 that means \"not entered\" (#774, part 1)","user":{"login":"datagen24","id":20876965,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwODc2OTY1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20876965?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/datagen24","html_url":"https://github.com/datagen24","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datagen24/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datagen24/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datagen24/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datagen24/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datagen24/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datagen24/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datagen24/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datagen24/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datagen24/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Part 1 of 2 for #774. Implements [ADR-0045](docs/adr/0045-an-unknown-stock-value-is-distinguishable-from-a-known-zero.md) gate 1 option (a) and open questions 6, 8, 9, 10 and 11. **ADR-0045 stays Proposed.** Part 2 (migration 0316) adds the readers, the `*_incomplete` flags (gate 5), accepted differences D1–D4 (gate 7) and the P2 write paths.\n\n**This part changes no API response.** The contract snapshots are unchanged. Merging it before part 2 is safe: no reader looks at the new marker yet.\n\n## Why\nUnder P2, which the maintainer chose, a price of `0` is a known zero and `null` is unknown. But earlier releases and grocy's purchase page stored `0` whenever the price field was left blank. So existing and imported zeros have to be read as unknown, without rewriting the stock ledger.\n\n## What changed\n- **Migration 0315**\n  - Adds `stock.legacy_zero_price` and `stock_log.legacy_zero_price`. Each is `SMALLINT NOT NULL DEFAULT 0`, constrained to 0 or 1, and allowed to be 1 only on a row priced exactly `0`.\n  - Marks every pre-existing zero through `mark_legacy_zero_prices('upgrade', 'unknown')`, which records the counts in a new `price_interpretation_reports` table (no row when there are no zeros). The cache-rebuilding `stock_log_UPD` trigger is held off for that one statement.\n  - `stock_next_use` and both of its INSTEAD OF triggers carry the marker. The view's columns are now written out instead of `s.*`: re-expanding `s.*` would also have started sending `stock.import_epoch` on the stock-entries routes, which the contract test caught. `stock_splits` groups by the marker.\n- **`StockService`:** copies the marker at all 19 sites that build a row from another row's price. Those are consume, transfer, open (including the remainder), measure, edit, and the undo rebuilds (consume, transfer, opening, edit, `InsertRowFromBooking`). An edit that supplies a price, explicit `0` included, makes it a known price.\n- **`DatabaseImporter`**\n  - Excludes the marker from the copied columns, so a source can't supply it.\n  - Marks imported zeros with the same function inside the copy transaction. That runs after verification, because the report row draws a sequence value that a rollback doesn't return; `import-tests` caught this.\n  - Prints the count, and records the policy in the report table, which is classified target-only.\n  - **`bin/victual-db-import`** gains `--legacy-zero-prices=unknown|known`, and now **refuses an unknown option** instead of silently ignoring it.\n- **`FieldPolicy::INTERNAL_FIELDS`** keeps the marker off every response for `stock`, `stock_log` and `stock_next_use`. Filter queries on it are refused like any redacted field.\n- **Docs:** the manual's import section and `docs/data-model.md` describe the marker and the report; ADR-0045 gains an Implementation section.\n- **Supporting changes:** the SQLite fixture gains the column, the difftest strips it, and `migratedifftest.php` lists the report table.\n\n## Tests\n- **`LegacyZeroPricePropagationTest`** (stockmaintenance phase), 9 tests: one per write path, each booking from a marked row, plus compaction keeping a marked `0` apart from a known `0`, plus the CHECKs. **7 fail with master's `StockService`.** The other two test the migration itself.\n- **`ImportLegacyZeroPricesTest`:** the default reads zeros as unknown, prices are copied unchanged, and the report and progress line appear. `known` leaves zeros known and records that. An invalid policy is refused.\n- **pgTAP `038-legacy-zero-price.sql`:** the constraints, `mark_legacy_zero_prices()` under both policies (including an upgrade with no zeros writing no report), the `stock_next_use` triggers, and `stock_splits`.\n- `WireContractTest` excludes `INTERNAL_FIELDS` from the relation columns it expects on the wire.\n- **Full local `.devtools/pgsql/run-tests.sh all` passed:** `SUITE PASSED`, 35 phases, PHP 8.5.10 / PostgreSQL 16. Contract snapshots unchanged; staged Vale 0 new findings.\n- **Not run:** PostgreSQL 15, the parity suite, and a migration timing test at ledger-generator scale.\n\nMigrations 0315 and 0316 are both claimed in `RESERVATIONS.md`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","created_at":"2026-10-18T16:50:48Z","updated_at":"2026-10-18T17:45:34Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"308f21e701c1661ce24ec4df8ab408175a7d9b20","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datagen24/victual/pulls/984/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datagen24/victual/pulls/984/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datagen24/victual/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/data